	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Usage

Browse your saved Ghostty layouts via the `layouts` keyword.

- &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Open the layout
- &lt;kbd&gt;⌘&lt;/kbd&gt;&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Edit the layout's file

A layout is a JSON file describing windows, tabs, splits, working directories and startup commands. They live in the folder set in the Workflow's Configuration, which defaults to `~/.config/alfred-ghostty-launch/configs`.

The first time you run the workflow it offers to create that folder along with an example layout to edit.

Layouts can also be opened from a script using the `launch` external trigger, passing the layout's file name without its extension.

Requires Ghostty 1.3 or later, which is the first version Alfred can drive directly.
</string>
